{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"dismantle","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"externalID":"s:9Ensembles16CoreDataEnsembleC9dismantleyyF","modules":[{"name":"Ensembles"}],"role":"symbol","title":"dismantle()","roleHeading":"Instance Method"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/dismantle()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dismantle"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Normally dismantling happens at deallocation. Call this explicitly when you need to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"create a replacement ensemble for the same store, to prevent two ensembles from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accessing the same data concurrently."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns at once. Captures stop and queued work is cancelled immediately. With no","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"operation running, the event store is closed before this returns, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replacement ensemble can open the same store straight away. While an operation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is running, it finishes its current step and the event store is closed on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"operation queue once it has, so the database is never taken away from work"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"still using it. A replacement ensemble created straight away opens the store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once the old operation’s current transaction ends, which blocks the creating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thread for that long. If an attach was running, wait for the old ensemble’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreDataEnsembleWillEndActivity"},{"type":"text","text":" notification before creating a replacement"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at the same local data root: a stopped attach removes the event store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directory it was building, as any failed attach does."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Forces the ensemble to dismantle, releasing all resources.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembles\/coredataensemble\/dismantle()"]}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CoreDataEnsemble/dismantle()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/dismantle()","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/coredataensemble\/dismantle()","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"dismantle()","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Forces the ensemble to dismantle, releasing all resources.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dismantle","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CoreDataEnsemble":{"title":"CoreDataEnsemble","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CoreDataEnsemble","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The central class of Ensembles, representing a set of synchronizing persistent stores."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/coredataensemble","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CoreDataEnsemble","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sync Core Data and SwiftData stores across devices using event sourcing."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"Ensembles","role":"collection"}}}